sses earning less than $500,000 a year are not covered by the state minimum.| Effective January 1, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $15.00 with maximum tip credit of $7.50 (50% of the applicable minimum wage).","Effective 01-01-2023.","Effective January 1st, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $15.16 with maximum tip credit of $3.02.","Effective January 1, 2026, a training wage rate of $9.31 (up from $9.08 in 2025) may be paid to employees less than 20 years old during the first 90 days of employment.","$14.20/$13.50 standard, rises to $15.45/$14.75 in Portland and drops to $13.20/$12.50 in non-urban counties as of 07-01-2023. Rises each July based upon the increase, if any, to the US City average Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers.","Same as federal minimum for employers with 10 or more full-time same-location employees or gross receipts of more than 100k per year. All other employees are subject to a minimum wage of $2.00, except those covered by FLSA, who are subject to federal minimum wage.","Effective 06-01-2023. Restaurant and hotel workers working a 7th consecutive day will have those hours treated as overtime.| Minors (Under 18) may be paid 85% of the minimum wage for their first 90 days of employment.| $6.38 - Tipped Wages for Wait Staff | $8.23 - Tipped Wages…","Starting July 1, 2024, a uniform minimum wage of $12.00 per hour for all employees is applicable.","Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $7.25 with maximum tip credit of $2.90 (40% of the applicable minimum wage).","Drops to $7.25 for employers with fewer than 4 employees. | Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $11.00 with maximum tip credit of $8.37.","Businesses that are not covered by the FLSA with gross annual sales of $110,000 or less are subject to a minimum wage of $4.00 per hour.","Effective 01-01-2023.","Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $7.25 with maximum tip credit of $3.90","Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $8.75 with maximum tip credit of $6.13 (70% of the applicable minimum wage).","Any employees that earn a guaranteed monthly compensation of $2,000 or more are exempt from minimum wage and overtime requirements.| Effective January 1, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $14.75 with maximum tip credit of $1.25.","Tipped wages are 55% of the applicable minimum wage. | Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $7.25 with maximum tip credit of $3.98 (45% of the applicable minimum wage).","Effective January 1, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $15.10 with maximum tip credit of $7.55 (50% of the applicable minimum wage).","Businesses that are not covered by the FLSA with gross annual sales of $110,000 or less are subject to a minimum wage of $4.00 per hour.","Effective January 1, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $16.00 with maximum tip credit of $12.11.","Combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $15.00 with maximum tip credit of $12.77.","Effective January 1, 2026, combined cash & tip minimum wage rate is $11.85 with maximum tip credit of $5.925 (50% of the applicable minimum wage).","Employers in Alaska that use an approved voluntary flexible work hour plan can schedule 10-hour days (40-hour weeks), and overtime pay would start after 10 hours per day instead of after 8. | Additionally, employers with fewer than 4 employees are not subject to daily or weekl…","Employers with 2 or more employees qualify for overtime, except for some industry-specific exemptions."]]},"24532":{"_":[[0,2,3,5,10,12,13,15,17,18,19,28,37,39,41,43,44,48],["x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x","x"]]}}}